<!--
  <sui-toast> — SUI port of <ship-toast>.
  Transient notification card with tone channel, auto-icon, hover-to-pause
  auto-dismiss, optional progress bar, and exit animation.

  Prop / event / method parity vs <ship-toast>
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                             SUI                      Notes
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  tone (Tone, undefined)          tone (union, 'default',  ✓ reflects; drives
                                    reflect)                 --tone-* + auto-icon
  size ('sm'|'md'|'lg', 'md')    size (union, 'md',       ✓ reflects
                                    reflect)
  duration (number, 5000)        duration (number, 5000)   ✓ property only; 0=persist
  dismissible (bool, true)        dismissible (bool,       ✓ reflects; shows close btn
                                    true, reflect)
  show-progress (bool, false)     show-progress (bool,     ✓ reflects
                                    false, reflect)
  closing (bool, false)           closing (bool,           ✓ reflects; set by close()
                                    false, reflect)          during exit animation
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Events: ship-dismiss            sui-dismiss              ✓ renamed; detail.reason
    (bubbles, composed)                                      'manual'|'timeout'|
                                                             'programmatic'
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  dismiss(reason?)                dismiss(reason?)         ✓ sync remove + event
  close(reason?)                  close(reason?)           ✓ animated, reduced-motion
                                                             aware
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Slots: icon, title, (default),  icon, title, (default),  ✓ same
    actions                         actions
  Parts: toast, close             toast, close             ✓ same (unchanged from
                                                             feat/next — no parts
                                                             added to inner anatomy)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ARIA: inner div role=status/    same on inner div        ✓ destructive+warning →
    alert, aria-live=polite/        (tone-driven)            role=alert, assertive
    assertive
  tabindex=0 on host              controller sets on host  ✓ if not already set
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - tone is the GLOBAL framework channel (TONES_CSS): no per-component <theme>
    block. `.toast`/`.icon` read var(--tone-bg)/var(--tone-fg) directly. The
    global channel's 'default' tone resolves to --tone-bg:hover-bg/--tone-
    border:border, which is NOT the flat card look this component wants for
    its untoned state — so the toast/icon variants blocks each carry ONE
    override (`tone=default: bg:surface-1 border:strong` /
    `bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground`) restoring the feat/next default look.
    Every other tone (info/success/warning/destructive/accent/primary/muted)
    needs no override — the global --tone-bg/--tone-border already equal the
    exact values feat/next hand-declared per tone.
  - Controller is BYTE-IDENTICAL to feat/next — no behavior changed, only the
    template's styling mechanism.
  - The dismiss control is a bare framework `<button ghost xs>` (22×22 via the
    xs size channel — an exact match for feat/next's hand-sized 22px close
    button) — no hand-styled `.close` background/hover/focus CSS. Per the
    alert pilot's PRECEDENTED deviation: the custom tone-tinted hover
    (`background:tone-bg` on hover) and the custom double-ring focus box-
    shadow are dropped in favor of the framework ghost skin's own hover/
    focus treatment (same trade the alert re-port already made and reported;
    not a new finding).
  - sx is closed-vocabulary (tokens + tone-*/size-* channels only); `<style>`
    keeps only what sx structurally cannot express: `display:grid` +
    `grid-template-columns` (grid isn't a `display:` sx keyword), `column-
    gap`/`row-gap` (gap is deliberately absent from sx — layout primitives'
    job, and `.toast` is a plain div here, same as sui-alert's `.box`),
    `padding-right` (calc() combining two tokens — sx has no calc), the
    `::before` tone stripe (pseudo-element), `.icon svg` compound-selector
    sizing, the close button's position OFFSETS (sx has `position:` the
    keyword but no `top`/`inset-inline-end`), `grid-column`, the progress
    bar's animation/keyframes/transform, and the two media queries.
  - min-width/max-width: feat/next's raw pixel pairs (280/420 · 240/360 ·
    320/460 for md/sm/lg) don't land exactly on the panel-min-w-*/panel-max-
    w-* scale. Snapped to the size-matched panel token (panel-min-w-{size} /
    panel-max-w-{size}) — the SAME quantization tokens.css already documents
    for sui-dialog (500px max-w → --panel-max-w-md/480px, "unifies onto"),
    not a new escape hatch. Not a LANG-GAP: the token scale trades exact
    pixels for a bounded palette by design; this is normal quantization, not
    a structural gap.
  - Icon box/glyph dimensions likewise snap to the nearest control-h-*/icon-
    size-* step (26→24 control-h-xs, 22→22 control-h-2xs exact, 30→28
    control-h-sm; 15→14 icon-size-sm, 13→12 icon-size-xs, 17→18 icon-size-lg)
    — the same rounding the alert pilot already applied to its own 26px icon
    box (→ control-h-xs).
  - Dropped: `--toast-slide-x`/`--toast-slide-y` custom properties. Dead code
    in the feat/next baseline itself — declared per `[data-slide-from]` value
    but never consumed anywhere (the `in:slide`/`out:fade` transition
    directives take their axis/duration from the inline directive argument,
    not a host custom property). Confirmed by grep across the feat/next tree
    before dropping; no behavior lost.
  - Stripe visibility simplified from 7 enumerated tone selectors to
    `:host(:not([tone='default']))` — behaviorally identical (tone is always
    one of the 8 reflected values; "not default" ≡ "one of the other 7").

  No new LANG-GAP. The control-skin gap the alert pilot surfaced (framework
  L1 buttons rendering unskinned inside shadow) is fixed at the runtime level
  (adoptSuiSheets now carries CONTROL_SKINS_CSS) — `<button ghost xs>` here
  paints correctly.
-->

<component>{
  props: {
    tone,
    size: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg',
    duration: 5000,
    dismissible: true,
    'show-progress': false,
    closing: false,
  },
}</component>

<variants class="toast">
  tone=default: bg:surface-1 border:strong
  size=sm: py:2_5 px:3 text:sm min-w:panel-min-w-sm max-w:panel-max-w-sm
  size=lg: py:3_5 px:4 text:md min-w:panel-min-w-lg max-w:panel-max-w-lg
</variants>

<variants class="icon">
  tone=default: bg:surface-1 fg:muted-foreground
  size=sm: w:control-h-2xs h:control-h-2xs
  size=lg: w:control-h-sm h:control-h-sm
</variants>

<variants class="body">
  [data-no-title]: fg:card-foreground
</variants>

<variants class="actions">
  [data-no-actions]: display:none
</variants>

<style>
  :host {
    display: block;
    pointer-events: auto;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
  :host([hidden]) { display: none; }

  .toast {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: start;
    column-gap: var(--space-2_5);
    row-gap: var(--space-1);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    padding-right: calc(var(--space-3_5) + var(--icon-size-2xl));
  }
  :host([size='sm']) .toast { column-gap: var(--space-2); padding-right: calc(var(--space-3) + var(--icon-size-2xl)); }
  :host([size='lg']) .toast { column-gap: var(--space-3); padding-right: calc(var(--space-4) + var(--icon-size-2xl)); }
  :host([data-no-icon]) .toast { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; }

  .toast::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    top: 0; bottom: 0;
    width: var(--space-1);
    background: var(--tone-fg);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  :host(:not([tone='default'])) .toast::before { opacity: 1; }

  .icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .icon svg { display: block; width: var(--icon-size-sm); height: var(--icon-size-sm); }
  :host([size='sm']) .icon svg { width: var(--icon-size-xs); height: var(--icon-size-xs); }
  :host([size='lg']) .icon svg { width: var(--icon-size-lg); height: var(--icon-size-lg); }
  :host([data-no-icon]) .icon { display: none; }

  .body { word-break: break-word; }
  :host([data-no-title]) .title { display: none; }

  .actions { grid-column: 2; }

  .close {
    top: var(--space-2);
    inset-inline-end: var(--space-2);
  }

  .progress {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    border-top-right-radius: var(--radius-full);
    transform: scaleX(1);
    transform-origin: left center;
    animation: sui-toast-progress var(--toast-duration) linear forwards;
  }
  :host(:hover) .progress,
  :host([data-paused]) .progress { animation-play-state: paused; }
  @keyframes sui-toast-progress {
    from { transform: scaleX(1); }
    to   { transform: scaleX(0); }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .progress { animation: none; }
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .toast { border: 1px solid CanvasText; }
    .close:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid CanvasText; outline-offset: 2px; }
  }
</style>


<controller>
import { controller, effect, ref, signal } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import type { ViewScope } from '@ship/sui-runtime'
import type { Scope } from './sui-toast.sui'

type DismissReason = 'manual' | 'timeout' | 'programmatic'

const TONES_WITH_AUTO_ICON = new Set(['info', 'success', 'warning', 'destructive', 'accent'])

export default controller({
  scope: (_ctx: ViewScope<Scope>) => {
    const hasSlottedIcon = signal(false)
    const visible = signal(true)
    const iconSlotEl = ref<HTMLSlotElement>(null)
    const titleSlotEl = ref<HTMLSlotElement>(null)
    const actionsSlotEl = ref<HTMLSlotElement>(null)
    const closeBtn = ref<HTMLButtonElement>(null)
    return { hasSlottedIcon, visible, iconSlotEl, titleSlotEl, actionsSlotEl, closeBtn }
  },

  mount(state, host) {
    let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null
    let remaining = 0
    let startedAt = 0
    let removed = false

    if (!host.hasAttribute('tabindex')) host.tabIndex = 0

    function clearTimer() {
      if (timer) { clearTimeout(timer); timer = null }
    }

    function scheduleDismiss() {
      clearTimer()
      const dur = state.duration as number
      if (dur > 0) {
        remaining = dur
        startedAt = Date.now()
        timer = setTimeout(() => dismiss('timeout'), dur)
        host.style.setProperty('--toast-duration', `${dur}ms`)
      }
    }

    function dismiss(reason: DismissReason = 'manual') {
      if (removed) return
      removed = true
      clearTimer()
      host.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sui-dismiss', {
        detail: { reason },
        bubbles: true,
        composed: true,
      }))
      host.remove()
    }

    async function close(reason: DismissReason = 'manual') {
      if (removed) return
      const prefersReduce =
        typeof window !== 'undefined' &&
        window.matchMedia?.('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches
      if (prefersReduce) {
        dismiss(reason)
        return
      }
      clearTimer()
      host.setAttribute('closing', '')
      // Flip `visible` to false; bindIf runs `out:fade` on the .toast
      // wrapper. The out-transition's duration (180ms — see template)
      // gates when we tear the host down.
      state.visible = false
      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 200))
      dismiss(reason)
    }

    const onPause = () => {
      if (!timer) return
      const elapsed = Date.now() - startedAt
      remaining = Math.max(0, remaining - elapsed)
      clearTimer()
      host.toggleAttribute('data-paused', true)
    }

    const onResume = () => {
      if (removed || (state.duration as number) <= 0) return
      if (remaining <= 0) return
      host.toggleAttribute('data-paused', false)
      startedAt = Date.now()
      timer = setTimeout(() => dismiss('timeout'), remaining)
    }

    const onKeydown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
      if (e.key === 'Escape' && state.dismissible) {
        e.stopPropagation()
        dismiss('manual')
      }
    }

    host.addEventListener('mouseenter', onPause)
    host.addEventListener('mouseleave', onResume)
    host.addEventListener('focusin', onPause)
    host.addEventListener('focusout', onResume)
    host.addEventListener('keydown', onKeydown)

    scheduleDismiss()

    const slotIsFilled = (slot: HTMLSlotElement): boolean =>
      slot.assignedNodes({ flatten: true }).some((n) => {
        if (n.nodeType === Node.ELEMENT_NODE) return true
        return (n.textContent?.trim().length ?? 0) > 0
      })

    const iconSlotEl = state.iconSlotEl as HTMLSlotElement | null
    if (iconSlotEl) {
      const onIconSlotChange = () => { state.hasSlottedIcon = slotIsFilled(iconSlotEl) }
      iconSlotEl.addEventListener('slotchange', onIconSlotChange)
      state.hasSlottedIcon = slotIsFilled(iconSlotEl)
    }

    const titleSlotEl = state.titleSlotEl as HTMLSlotElement | null
    const actionsSlotEl = state.actionsSlotEl as HTMLSlotElement | null

    if (titleSlotEl) {
      const onTitleChange = () =>
        host.toggleAttribute('data-no-title', !slotIsFilled(titleSlotEl))
      titleSlotEl.addEventListener('slotchange', onTitleChange)
      host.toggleAttribute('data-no-title', !slotIsFilled(titleSlotEl))
    }

    if (actionsSlotEl) {
      const onActionsChange = () =>
        host.toggleAttribute('data-no-actions', !slotIsFilled(actionsSlotEl))
      actionsSlotEl.addEventListener('slotchange', onActionsChange)
      host.toggleAttribute('data-no-actions', !slotIsFilled(actionsSlotEl))
    }

    const stopIconAttrEffect = effect(() => {
      const tone = state.tone
      const slotted = state.hasSlottedIcon
      const hasAuto = TONES_WITH_AUTO_ICON.has(tone as string)
      host.toggleAttribute('data-no-icon', !hasAuto && !slotted)
    })

    const stopCloseEffect = effect(() => {
      const btn = state.closeBtn
      if (!btn) return
      const onClick = () => dismiss('manual')
      btn.addEventListener('click', onClick)
      return () => btn.removeEventListener('click', onClick)
    })

    const h = host as HTMLElement & { dismiss: typeof dismiss; close: typeof close }
    h.dismiss = dismiss
    h.close = close

    return () => {
      removed = true
      clearTimer()
      host.removeEventListener('mouseenter', onPause)
      host.removeEventListener('mouseleave', onResume)
      host.removeEventListener('focusin', onPause)
      host.removeEventListener('focusout', onResume)
      host.removeEventListener('keydown', onKeydown)
      stopIconAttrEffect()
      stopCloseEffect()
    }
  },
})

</controller>
<!--
  `{#if visible()}` + asymmetric `in:slide` / `out:fade` drive the
  enter/exit polish. Controller flips `visible` to false in `close()`
  and the bindIf-driven out-transition keeps the toast in the DOM
  until the fade finishes (after which the controller calls
  `dismiss()` to remove the host).
-->
{#if visible()}
<div class="toast"
  in:slide={{ axis: 'y', duration: 200 }}
  out:fade={{ duration: 180 }}
  role={tone() === 'destructive' || tone() === 'warning' ? 'alert' : 'status'}
  aria-live={tone() === 'destructive' || tone() === 'warning' ? 'assertive' : 'polite'}
  aria-atomic="true"
  part="toast"
  sx="position:relative overflow:hidden radius:lg shadow:lg text:base leading:normal py:3 px:3_5 min-w:panel-min-w-md max-w:panel-max-w-md bg:tone-bg border:tone-border fg:card-foreground">
  <span class="icon"
    sx="w:control-h-xs h:control-h-xs radius:md bg:tone-bg fg:tone-fg">
    <slot name="icon" bind:this={iconSlotEl}></slot>
    {#if !hasSlottedIcon()}
      {#match tone()}
        {:case 'info'}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>
            <path d="M12 8h.01"/>
            <path d="M11 12h1v4h1"/>
          </svg>
        {:case 'success'}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>
            <path d="m8.5 12.5 2.5 2.5 4.5-5"/>
          </svg>
        {:case 'warning'}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0Z"/>
            <line x1="12" x2="12" y1="9" y2="13"/>
            <line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"/>
          </svg>
        {:case 'destructive'}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>
            <line x1="15" x2="9" y1="9" y2="15"/>
            <line x1="9" x2="15" y1="9" y2="15"/>
          </svg>
        {:case 'accent'}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 2 3 14h7l-1 8 10-12h-7l1-8Z"/>
          </svg>
      {/match}
    {/if}
  </span>
  <column class="content" gap="0" sx="min-w:0 fg:card-foreground">
    <div class="title" sx="weight:semibold tracking:tight leading:tight fg:foreground">
      <slot name="title" bind:this={titleSlotEl}></slot>
    </div>
    <div class="body" sx="fg:muted-foreground leading:normal">
      <slot></slot>
    </div>
    <row class="actions" gap="2" sx="mt:1_5">
      <slot name="actions" bind:this={actionsSlotEl}></slot>
    </row>
  </column>
  {#if dismissible()}
    <button ghost xs class="close" part="close" type="button" aria-label="Dismiss notification" bind:this={closeBtn}
      sx="position:absolute z:elevated">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" sx="w:icon-size-xs h:icon-size-xs">
        <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line>
        <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line>
      </svg>
    </button>
  {/if}
  {#if showProgress() && duration() > 0}
    <span class="progress" aria-hidden="true" sx="h:half bg:tone-fg"></span>
  {/if}
</div>
{/if}
